# Forum Category Mobile Layout

## Context
The category thread route allows its title column to shrink to zero while its
toolbar is non-shrinking. Narrow real-device viewports can therefore compress
the category name beneath the search controls even though the shared filter bar
has its own mobile rules. The route also expands and retracts the full forum on
mount, causing an avoidable layout shift.

## Goal
- Keep the category identity and controls readable and non-overlapping on narrow
  and coarse-pointer mobile browsers.
- Preserve the optional forum expander without an automatic mount transition.

## Non-Goals
- Redesign the forum directory or thread table.
- Change forum APIs, permissions, or realtime behavior.

## Steps
1. Move the category header and expander layout into route-scoped CSS.
2. Stack the title and toolbar at the shared mobile breakpoint and constrain all
   flex children to the available inline size.
3. Start the optional forum directory collapsed and remove the timed layout shift.
4. Add focused component coverage and run frontend quality gates.

## Verification
